7","site":"T Nation · 3979 posts · 2023"},{"title":"Brute's Book","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/brutes-book/210950","site":"T Nation · 2469 posts · 2015"},{"title":"WannaBe’s Last Year Of “DYEL?”","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/wannabe-s-last-year-of-dyel/268239","site":"T Nation · 2227 posts · 2020"},{"title":"The Andrew Tate Case","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/the-andrew-tate-case/280860","site":"T Nation · 1274 posts · 2023"},{"title":"Single Moms!","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/single-moms/287396","site":"T Nation · 1074 posts · 2024"},{"title":"Happy Marriages/Relationships","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/happy-marriages-relationships/263355","site":"T Nation · 923 posts · 2019"},{"title":"Do You Still Believe in the United States?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/do-you-still-believe-in-the-united-states/288619","site":"T Nation · 708 posts · 2024"},{"title":"More Women in Power?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/more-women-in-power/275230","site":"T Nation · 648 posts · 2021"},{"title":"I Wanna Talk about How to Get a Girlfriend","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/i-wanna-talk-about-how-to-get-a-girlfriend/270948","site":"T Nation · 631 posts · 2020"},{"title":"A cautionary tale for those who identify with the Democratic Party","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/a-cautionary-tale-for-those-who-identify-with-the-democratic-party/288532","site":"T Nation · 557 posts · 2024"},{"title":"Women's Fight to Vote Tied to Declining SMV","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/womens-fight-to-vote-tied-to-declining-smv/183728","site":"T Nation · 549 posts · 2012"},{"title":"did a few hours of research most realistic colored contacts by far","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/did-a-few-hours-of-research-most-realistic-colored-contacts-by-far.142649/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20210910055547/https://looksmax.org/threads/did-a-few-hours-of-research-most-realistic-colored-contacts-by-far.142649/"},{"title":"volcel if youre not wearing colored contacts","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/volcel-if-youre-not-wearing-colored-contacts.7528/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220930092829/https://looksmax.org/threads/volcel-if-youre-not-wearing-colored-contacts.7528/"}],"web":[{"title":"Circle contact lens — Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circle_contact_lens"}]},"wikipedia":{"title":"Circle contact lens","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circle_contact_lens"},"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Colored contact lenses, also called cosmetic, decorative or fashion lenses, change the apparent colour of the eye. Circle lenses, also called big-eye lenses, are a type of cosmetic lens that adds a coloured or dark ring to enlarge the apparent size of the iris. [1]","In the United States the Food and Drug Administration regulates decorative lenses as medical devices, requires a prescription for them, and warns that lenses obtained without a proper fitting can cause corneal abrasion, allergic reactions, reduced vision and infections that may lead to blindness.","In looksmaxxing communities, coloured lenses are discussed as a way to lighten or contrast the eye colour, especially for people with dark brown eyes, and users debate shades, wear time and whether the result looks natural. No controlled study of their effect on perceived attractiveness was found. [2][3]"],"infobox":[["Type","Cosmetic / decorative contact lens (tinted or patterned)"],["Also known as","Circle lenses, big-eye lenses, fashion lenses, theatre lenses [1]"],["US regulation","Medical device; prescription required"],["Known hazard","Some circle lenses contain iron oxide and other metals, a potential MRI hazard [1]"],["Main risks (FDA)","Corneal abrasion, allergy, reduced vision, infection"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["Cosmetic lenses can be plano (no vision correction) or made with a prescription. They may tint the iris colour, print an opaque pattern, or add a darker or larger rim in the case of circle lenses, which are intended to make the eyes appear bigger. [1] A report published in BMC Medical Imaging notes that circle lenses usually contain iron oxide and other metals in their pigment, which is why they may be a hazard during magnetic resonance imaging. [1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Regulation and safety","paras":["The FDA states that decorative contact lenses are medical devices that must be prescribed by a doctor, with the prescription listing the brand, lens measurements and expiry date. It advises buying only from sellers that require a prescription and sell FDA-cleared lenses, and it names street vendors, beauty-supply and novelty shops and unknown online sellers as sources of potentially contaminated or counterfeit products.","The agency lists corneal abrasion, allergic reaction, decreased vision and infection as risks of lenses worn without a proper fit or prescription, and advises seeking an eye doctor immediately for redness, persistent eye pain or reduced vision. It also advises against sharing lenses.","Case reporting adds a specific imaging concern: a published case described the incidental discovery of circle lenses on an MRI scan, with the authors noting the metal content of the pigment. [1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No clinical trials of coloured or circle lenses as an appearance intervention were found. The published literature on them consists mainly of case reports such as the MRI report. [1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Use in looksmaxxing communities","paras":["Forum threads ask which colours suit a particular complexion and hair colour, and how to get a green or hazel result over dark brown eyes while keeping a natural look. One poster lists requirements of light green or hazel colour, a natural appearance, a pupil opening that does not obscure vision, and longer wear times. [2] Another asks whether lenses can be ordered online without knowing eye measurements. [3] Thread titles include claims that lenses are a large 'ascension', that wearing them is the 'ultimate cope', and personal accounts of what lenses did for the poster. [4][5][6]"],"subs":[]}],"lore":{"intro":"Community discussion focuses on shade selection and on whether coloured lenses meaningfully raise attractiveness. [2][4][5]","claims":[{"claim":"Lighter eye colour from lenses gives a noticeable increase in looks","verdict":"unknown","note":""},{"claim":"Lenses can be bought online without an eye exam or measurements","verdict":"unknown","note":""},{"claim":"Coloured lenses are a 'cope' that does not help","verdict":"unknown","note":""}]},"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"Incidental discovery of circle contact lens by MRI: you can't scan my poker face, circle contact lens as a potential MRI hazard","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23530981/","source":"BMC Medical Imaging","year":2013,"type":"study"},{"title":"COLORED CONTACTS? (PICS)","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/colored-contacts-pics.1264839/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2022,"type":"forum"},{"title":"Colored contacts","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/colored-contacts.591001/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2020,"type":"forum"},{"title":"how much ascension are colored contacts","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/how-much-ascension-are-colored-contacts.457539/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2019,"type":"forum"},{"title":"what colored contacts did for me","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/what-colored-contacts-did-for-me.1271978/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2022,"type":"forum"},{"title":"wearing colored contacts is the ultimate cope","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/wearing-colored-contacts-is-the-ultimate-cope.900201/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2021,"type":"forum"}],"studies":[{"title":"Incidental discovery of circle contact lens by MRI: you can't scan my poker face, circle contact lens as a potential MRI hazard","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23530981/","source":"BMC Medical Imaging","year":2013,"kind":null}],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Colored Contact